#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-SD0005 expect=skipped domain=LB
#note "LBSEQ is not in the dataset (rule round 2026-10-12, var_exists sweep): there is no --SEQ value to be unique, so the rule is SKIPPED by Requirements.Variables.All, which replaced the Check-level var_exists(\"--SEQ\") guard (the absence itself is reported once by CDISC-CG0313-B / CG0554-B). Red under the old rule (it ran and passed silently), and red under a bare removal: an absent --SEQ drops out of the [--SEQ, DOMAIN, USUBJID] key, so subject 001's two records would read as duplicates."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
dataset LB class=FINDINGS label="Laboratory Test Results"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col LBTESTCD type=Char label="Lab Test Short Name"
---
S1 | LB | 001 | ALB
S1 | LB | 001 | GLUC
S1 | LB | 002 | ALB
